<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <!--
      Deliberately no INTERNET permission here: this is the release
      manifest, and the app's core privacy claim is that it never requests
      network access. Metro's dev-server permission lives ONLY in
      src/debug/AndroidManifest.xml, merged into debug builds, never release.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.CAMERA" />

    <application
      android:name=".MainApplication"
      android:label="@string/app_name"
      android:icon="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
      android:roundIcon="@mipmap/ic_launcher_round"
      android:allowBackup="false"
      android:theme="@style/AppTheme"
      android:usesCleartextTraffic="${usesCleartextTraffic}"
      android:supportsRtl="true">
      <!--
        libOpenCL.so access is deliberately NOT declared here right now;
        see HISTORY below for when it was, and why it's off again.

        REQUIRES a supported Adreno/OpenCL tier (verified safe: Adreno 825
        on a Nothing Phone 3, Snapdragon 8s Gen 4). CONFIRMED UNSAFE on a
        Snapdragon 778G+ / Adreno 642L device (2026-08-16): OpenCL backend
        registration called ggml_abort(), a hard SIGABRT crash, not a
        graceful fallback, because that GPU isn't in llama.cpp's supported
        tier. This is a single shared manifest with no runtime chip-tier
        detection, so installing a build with this declared on unsupported
        hardware WILL crash on model load. Do not ship broadly with this
        declared until that gap is closed (runtime capability check, or
        confirmation from a newer llama.rn that registration fails
        gracefully instead of aborting).

        HISTORY: on the Nothing Phone 3, this measured 18.8-31s extractions
        with exact-match accuracy across two sessions (2026-08-16,
        2026-08-24; the latter after a thermal-throttling false alarm in
        between, see CLAUDE.md's mobile caveat section for that full
        evidence chain). REMOVED AGAIN on 2026-08-31 before ever installing
        on a third test device (a HONOR REA-NX9): `/sys/class/kgsl/kgsl-3d0/gpu_model`
        reports Adreno 644, `ro.vendor.qti.soc_id` reports SM7450
        (Snapdragon 7 Gen 1), a mid-range 6-series Adreno GPU in the same
        family as the 642L that already confirmed-crashed, not the
        750+/8-series flagship tier the accelerated path is verified safe
        on. Disabled pre-emptively rather than risk-testing the crash on
        real hardware; CPU-only fallback (the code path this absence
        forces) is the one to verify working on this device.
      -->
      <activity
        android:name=".MainActivity"
        android:label="@string/app_name"
        android:configChanges="keyboard|keyboardHidden|orientation|screenLayout|screenSize|smallestScreenSize|uiMode"
        android:launchMode="singleTask"
        android:windowSoftInputMode="adjustResize"
        android:exported="true">
        <intent-filter>
            <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />
            <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
        </intent-filter>
      </activity>
    </application>
</manifest>
